Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='plugins', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='A plugin is one function and its grant: a WebAssembly component whose one import of ours is fetch', body="⚠️ *A plugin is one function and its grant* (2026-10-24; `suzatary-plugin`, `suzatary_core::plugin`). A plugin is a WebAssembly component of `app/wit/plugin.wit`'s `source` world: `sync(cursor, credentials)` returns items and the next cursor, and its one import of ours is `fetch`. Built for wasm32-wasip2, it also imports WASI's clocks, random numbers and standard streams, which the host links with nothing in them (an empty environment and stdin, a bounded stderr, the box's own clocks); the host links no WASI filesystem or sockets, so `Host::load` refuses a component importing either before it runs. `fetch` is the host's: the `[[plugins]]` manifest (`name`, `component`, `schema`, `origins`, `credentials`) parses only to the origins it allows and to credential NAMES in `PLUGIN_<NAME>_` (so the app's own keys are outside any manifest's reach); a credential's value is a URL, which the host resolves through the secret effect and requests only at an allowed origin and only over https or loopback, so a plugin never holds one, and an answer that echoes it, or its path or query, is withheld (`Refusal::Echoed`). A call makes at most `MAX_FETCHES` (64). Each call is a fresh store under a time and memory `Budget`, stopped with a typed `RunError`; the host links its own monotonic clock, whose every wait ends at the call's deadline, since a wait blocks in the host where the epoch never fires; whatever the host keeps or prints of a plugin's words is `plugin::Said`, at most 512 bytes. The transport bounds every plugin: the deployment passes `Ureq::public_only()` (no redirect, no name resolving off the public internet, so never this box or the tailnet). The fences are `app/plugin/tests/fence.rs`, run by name against the hostile `app/plugin-fence` the flake builds and against the reference plugin.", rationale='Decided 2026-10-24.', supersedes=()))